    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This explains the previous article’s successful query: the analyst joined a group with database read privileges. Both current configuration and the process that produced it were available."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. Evidence for Explaining Access Decisions"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Evaluators need not only correct privileges but explanations later: security reviews ask who changed what and when; handovers ask how the current state arose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "QueryPie retained answers: search actions by group name, identify added users in details, and inspect the target connection and scope in database access logs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Providing privilege configuration together with records that trace it"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " stood out. Shared operations can rely on recorded actions rather than memory alone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
